Chapter: Klondike
  cites Games chapter Rng
  cites Foreword chapter Random

 Klondike, the solitaire everybody means by "solitaire". Fifty-two cards,
 seven tableau columns holding one to seven cards with only the last of each
 face up, a stock of twenty-four turned one or three at a time, and four
 foundations built ace upward in suit.

 It is the opposite game to Spider in the one way that matters to the code:
 Spider builds DOWN in suit and sends a finished run away by itself, while
 Klondike builds down in ALTERNATING COLOUR in the tableau and up in suit on
 the foundations, so the foundations are real piles a card is placed on and
 not a counter. That is why this chapter has `founds` and Spider has
 `completed-suits`.

 THE ACE IS LOW, and the fold that makes it so is the same one Spider needs
 and for the same reason: a card id carries its rank as `id mod 13` and that
 encoding is the page's, where 12 is the ace because every other card game in
 the arcade wants an ace-high deck. Here the ace is the bottom of a
 foundation and the bottom of a tableau run, so 12 folds to 0 and every other
 rank shifts up one. Without the fold the ace ranks above the king, no
 foundation can start, and no ace can be laid on a deuce.

 Face-down cards are counted, not marked. `downs` holds, per column, how many
 of the cards at the HEAD of that column are face down; a card at index below
 that count has not been seen by the player. Removing the last face-up card
 of a column turns the next one over, which is the flip, and the flip is the
 whole engine of the game: it is the only way hidden information becomes
 known.

 We say:

Section: Types

  KlondikeState = record {
    col0    : List Integer,
    col1    : List Integer,
    col2    : List Integer,
    col3    : List Integer,
    col4    : List Integer,
    col5    : List Integer,
    col6    : List Integer,
    downs   : List Integer,
    founds  : List Integer,
    stock   : List Integer,
    waste   : List Integer,
    draw    : Integer,
    sterile : Integer,
    moves   : Integer
  }

  KlondikeResult = record {
    founded : Integer,
    moves   : Integer,
    won     : Boolean
  }

  KlondikeMove = record {
    from  : Integer,
    start : Integer,
    to    : Integer
  }

Section: Card Helpers

 Rank 0 is the ace and rank 12 the king, which is the fold described above.

  kd-rank : Integer -> Integer
  kd-rank (c) =
    let r = rng-mod c 13
    in if r == 12 then 0 else r + 1

  kd-suit : Integer -> Integer
  kd-suit (c) = c / 13

 Suits 1 and 2 are hearts and diamonds, which is the page's `SUIT` order.
 The tableau cares only whether two cards differ in colour, never which
 colour either one is.

  kd-red : Integer -> Boolean
  kd-red (c) =
    let s = kd-suit c
    in if s == 1 then True else if s == 2 then True else False

  kd-alternates : Integer, Integer -> Boolean
  kd-alternates (a) (b) =
    if kd-red a then if kd-red b then False else True
    else if kd-red b then True else False

Section: Small List Helpers

  kd-take-loop : List Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, List Integer -> List Integer
  kd-take-loop (src) (start) (count) (i) (acc) =
    if i >= count then acc
    else kd-take-loop src start count (i + 1) (list-push acc (list-at src (start + i)))

  kd-slice : List Integer, Integer, Integer -> List Integer
  kd-slice (src) (start) (count) = kd-take-loop src start count 0 []

  kd-copy-of : List Integer -> List Integer
  kd-copy-of (src) = kd-take-loop src 0 (list-length src) 0 []

  kd-drop-from-end : List Integer, Integer -> List Integer
  kd-drop-from-end (src) (count) =
    let n = list-length src
    in kd-take-loop src 0 (n - count) 0 []

  kd-append : List Integer, List Integer, Integer, Integer -> List Integer
  kd-append (base) (extra) (i) (n) =
    if i >= n then base
    else kd-append (list-push base (list-at extra i)) extra (i + 1) n

  kd-fill : Integer, Integer, Integer, List Integer -> List Integer
  kd-fill (v) (i) (n) (acc) =
    if i >= n then acc
    else kd-fill v (i + 1) n (list-push acc v)

  kd-count-up : Integer, Integer, List Integer -> List Integer
  kd-count-up (i) (n) (acc) =
    if i >= n then acc
    else kd-count-up (i + 1) n (list-push acc i)

 The waste turned back into a stock is the pile flipped over, so the card
 that went to the waste first is the one that comes off the stock first.

  kd-reverse-loop : List Integer, Integer, List Integer -> List Integer
  kd-reverse-loop (src) (i) (acc) =
    if i < 0 then acc
    else kd-reverse-loop src (i - 1) (list-push acc (list-at src i))

  kd-reverse : List Integer -> List Integer
  kd-reverse (src) = kd-reverse-loop src (list-length src - 1) []

Section: Deck Building

  klondike-deck-new : Integer -> List Integer
  klondike-deck-new (seed) =
    let deck = kd-count-up 0 52 []
    in kd-shuffle deck seed 51

  kd-shuffle : List Integer, Integer, Integer -> List Integer
  kd-shuffle (deck) (seed) (i) =
    if i <= 0 then deck
    else let rng = rng-new (seed * 7 + i)
    in let j = rng-mod (rng-value (rng-next rng)) (i + 1)
    in let vi = list-at deck i
    in let vj = list-at deck j
    in let d2 = list-set-at deck i vj
    in let d3 = list-set-at d2 j vi
    in kd-shuffle d3 seed (i - 1)

Section: State Access

  kd-get-col : KlondikeState, Integer -> List Integer
  kd-get-col (st) (c) =
    if c == 0 then st.col0
    else if c == 1 then st.col1
    else if c == 2 then st.col2
    else if c == 3 then st.col3
    else if c == 4 then st.col4
    else if c == 5 then st.col5
    else st.col6

  kd-set-col : KlondikeState, Integer, List Integer -> KlondikeState
  kd-set-col (st) (c) (col) =
    if c == 0 then KlondikeState { col0 = col, col1 = st.col1, col2 = st.col2, col3 = st.col3,
                                   col4 = st.col4, col5 = st.col5, col6 = st.col6,
                                   downs = st.downs, founds = st.founds, stock = st.stock,
                                   waste = st.waste, draw = st.draw, sterile = st.sterile,
                                   moves = st.moves }
    else if c == 1 then KlondikeState { col0 = st.col0, col1 = col, col2 = st.col2, col3 = st.col3,
                                        col4 = st.col4, col5 = st.col5, col6 = st.col6,
                                        downs = st.downs, founds = st.founds, stock = st.stock,
                                        waste = st.waste, draw = st.draw, sterile = st.sterile,
                                        moves = st.moves }
    else if c == 2 then KlondikeState { col0 = st.col0, col1 = st.col1, col2 = col, col3 = st.col3,
                                        col4 = st.col4, col5 = st.col5, col6 = st.col6,
                                        downs = st.downs, founds = st.founds, stock = st.stock,
                                        waste = st.waste, draw = st.draw, sterile = st.sterile,
                                        moves = st.moves }
    else if c == 3 then KlondikeState { col0 = st.col0, col1 = st.col1, col2 = st.col2, col3 = col,
                                        col4 = st.col4, col5 = st.col5, col6 = st.col6,
                                        downs = st.downs, founds = st.founds, stock = st.stock,
                                        waste = st.waste, draw = st.draw, sterile = st.sterile,
                                        moves = st.moves }
    else if c == 4 then KlondikeState { col0 = st.col0, col1 = st.col1, col2 = st.col2, col3 = st.col3,
                                        col4 = col, col5 = st.col5, col6 = st.col6,
                                        downs = st.downs, founds = st.founds, stock = st.stock,
                                        waste = st.waste, draw = st.draw, sterile = st.sterile,
                                        moves = st.moves }
    else if c == 5 then KlondikeState { col0 = st.col0, col1 = st.col1, col2 = st.col2, col3 = st.col3,
                                        col4 = st.col4, col5 = col, col6 = st.col6,
                                        downs = st.downs, founds = st.founds, stock = st.stock,
                                        waste = st.waste, draw = st.draw, sterile = st.sterile,
                                        moves = st.moves }
    else KlondikeState { col0 = st.col0, col1 = st.col1, col2 = st.col2, col3 = st.col3,
                         col4 = st.col4, col5 = st.col5, col6 = col,
                         downs = st.downs, founds = st.founds, stock = st.stock,
                         waste = st.waste, draw = st.draw, sterile = st.sterile,
                         moves = st.moves }

 Everything that is not a column changes through one place, so a new field
 is added to this record in two spots rather than nine.

  kd-set-rest : KlondikeState, List Integer, List Integer, List Integer, List Integer, Integer, Integer -> KlondikeState
  kd-set-rest (st) (downs) (founds) (stock) (waste) (sterile) (moves) =
    KlondikeState { col0 = st.col0, col1 = st.col1, col2 = st.col2, col3 = st.col3,
                    col4 = st.col4, col5 = st.col5, col6 = st.col6,
                    downs = downs, founds = founds, stock = stock,
                    waste = waste, draw = st.draw, sterile = sterile,
                    moves = moves }

  kd-down-at : KlondikeState, Integer -> Integer
  kd-down-at (st) (c) = list-at (st.downs) c

  kd-found-at : KlondikeState, Integer -> Integer
  kd-found-at (st) (s) = list-at (st.founds) s

Section: Construction

  klondike-new : Integer, Integer -> KlondikeState
  klondike-new (seed) (draw) =
    let d = if draw < 1 then 1 else if draw > 3 then 3 else draw
    in kd-deal (klondike-deck-new seed) d

 Column i holds i + 1 cards and i of them are face down, so the deal walks
 the deck 1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7 and the twenty-four that are left are the
 stock.

  kd-deal : List Integer, Integer -> KlondikeState
  kd-deal (deck) (d) =
    let c0 = kd-slice deck 0 1
    in let c1 = kd-slice deck 1 2
    in let c2 = kd-slice deck 3 3
    in let c3 = kd-slice deck 6 4
    in let c4 = kd-slice deck 10 5
    in let c5 = kd-slice deck 15 6
    in let c6 = kd-slice deck 21 7
    in let stock = kd-slice deck 28 24
    in KlondikeState { col0 = c0, col1 = c1, col2 = c2, col3 = c3,
                       col4 = c4, col5 = c5, col6 = c6,
                       downs = kd-count-up 0 7 [], founds = kd-fill (-1) 0 4 [],
                       stock = stock, waste = [], draw = d, sterile = 0,
                       moves = 0 }

Section: Reading The Board

 A face-down card is not readable. The engine holds the truth and answers
 -1 for anything the player has not turned over, so a page cannot show a
 card the game has not dealt face up.

  kd-visible-card : KlondikeState, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  kd-visible-card (st) (c) (i) =
    let col = kd-get-col st c
    in if i < 0 then (-1)
    else if i >= list-length col then (-1)
    else if i < kd-down-at st c then (-1)
    else list-at col i

  kd-waste-top : KlondikeState -> Integer
  kd-waste-top (st) =
    let n = list-length (st.waste)
    in if n == 0 then (-1) else list-at (st.waste) (n - 1)

  kd-founded : KlondikeState, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  kd-founded (st) (s) (acc) =
    if s >= 4 then acc
    else kd-founded st (s + 1) (acc + kd-found-at st s + 1)

  kd-won : KlondikeState -> Boolean
  kd-won (st) = if kd-founded st 0 0 == 52 then True else False

Section: Sequence Logic

 A run that may be lifted off the tableau is face up, descends by one rank a
 card, and alternates colour. `kd-run-len` measures forward from an index to
 the end of the column and answers how many cards form such a run; a lift is
 legal only when that run reaches the END of the column, which is what stops
 a page carrying off an arbitrary handful.

  kd-run-len : List Integer, Integer -> Integer
  kd-run-len (col) (from-idx) =
    let n = list-length col
    in if from-idx >= n then 0
    else kd-run-walk col from-idx (from-idx + 1) 1

  kd-run-walk : List Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  kd-run-walk (col) (prev) (i) (len) =
    let n = list-length col
    in if i >= n then len
    else let c-prev = list-at col prev
    in let c-curr = list-at col i
    in if kd-rank c-curr /= kd-rank c-prev - 1 then len
    else if kd-alternates c-prev c-curr == False then len
    else kd-run-walk col i (i + 1) (len + 1)

Section: Legality

 `from` names where the cards come from: 0 to 6 a tableau column, 7 the
 waste, 8 to 11 a foundation. `to` names where they go: 0 to 6 a tableau
 column, 7 to 10 a foundation. A foundation takes one card and gives one
 back, which is legal Klondike and occasionally the only way out.

  kd-move-head : KlondikeState, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  kd-move-head (st) (from) (start) =
    if from == 7 then kd-waste-top st
    else if from >= 8 then kd-found-card st (from - 8)
    else kd-visible-card st from start

 A foundation's top card is its suit and its recorded rank, rebuilt into a
 card id. Rank 0 is the ace, whose id ends in 12, which is the fold again.

  kd-found-card : KlondikeState, Integer -> Integer
  kd-found-card (st) (s) =
    let r = kd-found-at st s
    in if r < 0 then (-1)
    else if r == 0 then s * 13 + 12
    else s * 13 + r - 1

  kd-count-moved : KlondikeState, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  kd-count-moved (st) (from) (start) =
    if from >= 7 then 1
    else list-length (kd-get-col st from) - start

 The destination test, and it is the whole difference from Spider: a tableau
 column takes a KING on an empty space and otherwise a card one rank below
 its top card and of the other colour, while a foundation takes the next
 rank up in its own suit and starts on an ace.

  kd-tableau-takes : KlondikeState, Integer, Integer -> Boolean
  kd-tableau-takes (st) (to) (card) =
    let col = kd-get-col st to
    in let n = list-length col
    in if n == 0 then (if kd-rank card == 12 then True else False)
    else let top = list-at col (n - 1)
    in if kd-rank card /= kd-rank top - 1 then False
    else kd-alternates top card

  kd-foundation-takes : KlondikeState, Integer, Integer -> Boolean
  kd-foundation-takes (st) (s) (card) =
    if kd-suit card /= s then False
    else let r = kd-found-at st s
    in if kd-rank card == r + 1 then True else False

 A tableau column may not be its own destination. `from` and `to` do NOT
 share a numbering -- 7 is the waste as a source and the spade foundation as
 a destination -- so this compares them only where both mean a column.
 Comparing them everywhere refuses the waste-to-spades move, which is one of
 the commonest moves in the game.

  kd-can-move : KlondikeState, Integer, Integer, Integer -> Boolean
  kd-can-move (st) (from) (start) (to) =
    if from < 0 then False
    else if from > 11 then False
    else if to < 0 then False
    else if to > 10 then False
    else let head = kd-move-head st from start
    in if head < 0 then False
    else if from < 7 then
      (if to < 7 then (if from == to then False else kd-can-from-tableau st from start to head)
       else kd-can-from-tableau st from start to head)
    else kd-can-single st from to head

 Lifting off a column: the cards from `start` to the end must be face up and
 must themselves be a run, or a page could carry off any handful it liked.
 More than one card may never go to a foundation.

  kd-can-from-tableau : KlondikeState, Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer -> Boolean
  kd-can-from-tableau (st) (from) (start) (to) (head) =
    let col = kd-get-col st from
    in let n = list-length col
    in if start < kd-down-at st from then False
    else if kd-run-len col start /= n - start then False
    else if to >= 7 then (if n - start /= 1 then False else kd-foundation-takes st (to - 7) head)
    else kd-tableau-takes st to head

  kd-can-single : KlondikeState, Integer, Integer, Integer -> Boolean
  kd-can-single (st) (from) (to) (head) =
    if to >= 7 then (if from >= 8 then False else kd-foundation-takes st (to - 7) head)
    else kd-tableau-takes st to head

Section: Move Execution

  kd-apply-move : KlondikeState, Integer, Integer, Integer -> KlondikeState
  kd-apply-move (st) (from) (start) (to) =
    let head = kd-move-head st from start
    in let count = kd-count-moved st from start
    in let moved = kd-lifted st from start count
    in let st2 = kd-remove-from st from start count
    in let st3 = kd-place-on st2 to moved count
    in let gained = if to >= 7 then 1 else 0
    in kd-after-move st3 from gained

  kd-lifted : KlondikeState, Integer, Integer, Integer -> List Integer
  kd-lifted (st) (from) (start) (count) =
    if from == 7 then kd-fill (kd-waste-top st) 0 1 []
    else if from >= 8 then kd-fill (kd-found-card st (from - 8)) 0 1 []
    else kd-slice (kd-get-col st from) start count

  kd-remove-from : KlondikeState, Integer, Integer, Integer -> KlondikeState
  kd-remove-from (st) (from) (start) (count) =
    if from == 7 then kd-set-rest st (st.downs) (st.founds) (st.stock) (kd-drop-from-end (st.waste) 1) (st.sterile) (st.moves)
    else if from >= 8 then kd-take-off-foundation st (from - 8)
    else kd-set-col st from (kd-drop-from-end (kd-get-col st from) count)

  kd-take-off-foundation : KlondikeState, Integer -> KlondikeState
  kd-take-off-foundation (st) (s) =
    let f2 = list-set-at (kd-copy-of (st.founds)) s (kd-found-at st s - 1)
    in kd-set-rest st (st.downs) f2 (st.stock) (st.waste) (st.sterile) (st.moves)

  kd-place-on : KlondikeState, Integer, List Integer, Integer -> KlondikeState
  kd-place-on (st) (to) (moved) (count) =
    if to >= 7 then kd-put-on-foundation st (to - 7) (list-at moved 0)
    else kd-set-col st to (kd-append (kd-get-col st to) moved 0 count)

  kd-put-on-foundation : KlondikeState, Integer, Integer -> KlondikeState
  kd-put-on-foundation (st) (s) (card) =
    let f2 = list-set-at (kd-copy-of (st.founds)) s (kd-rank card)
    in kd-set-rest st (st.downs) f2 (st.stock) (st.waste) (st.sterile) (st.moves)

 The flip. A column whose face-down count has reached its length has just
 had its last face-up card taken, so the next one turns over. This is the
 only place hidden information becomes known, which is why it also resets
 the sterile counter: a flip is progress even when nothing reached a
 foundation.

  kd-after-move : KlondikeState, Integer, Integer -> KlondikeState
  kd-after-move (st) (from) (gained) =
    let flipped = if from < 7 then kd-flip-needed st from else False
    in let d2 = if flipped then kd-flip st from else st.downs
    in let fresh = if gained > 0 then 0 else if flipped then 0 else st.sterile + 1
    in kd-set-rest st d2 (st.founds) (st.stock) (st.waste) fresh (st.moves + 1)

  kd-flip-needed : KlondikeState, Integer -> Boolean
  kd-flip-needed (st) (c) =
    let n = list-length (kd-get-col st c)
    in if n == 0 then False
    else if kd-down-at st c >= n then True
    else False

  kd-flip : KlondikeState, Integer -> List Integer
  kd-flip (st) (c) =
    let n = list-length (kd-get-col st c)
    in list-set-at (kd-copy-of (st.downs)) c (n - 1)

Section: The Stock

  kd-can-draw : KlondikeState -> Boolean
  kd-can-draw (st) = if list-length (st.stock) > 0 then True else False

  kd-draw : KlondikeState -> KlondikeState
  kd-draw (st) =
    if kd-can-draw st == False then st
    else kd-draw-loop st 0 (st.draw)

  kd-draw-loop : KlondikeState, Integer, Integer -> KlondikeState
  kd-draw-loop (st) (i) (n) =
    if i >= n then kd-set-rest st (st.downs) (st.founds) (st.stock) (st.waste) (st.sterile + 1) (st.moves + 1)
    else let sn = list-length (st.stock)
    in if sn == 0 then kd-set-rest st (st.downs) (st.founds) (st.stock) (st.waste) (st.sterile + 1) (st.moves + 1)
    else let card = list-at (st.stock) (sn - 1)
    in let st2 = kd-set-rest st (st.downs) (st.founds) (kd-drop-from-end (st.stock) 1) (list-push (kd-copy-of (st.waste)) card) (st.sterile) (st.moves)
    in kd-draw-loop st2 (i + 1) n

  kd-can-recycle : KlondikeState -> Boolean
  kd-can-recycle (st) =
    if list-length (st.stock) > 0 then False
    else if list-length (st.waste) == 0 then False
    else True

  kd-recycle : KlondikeState -> KlondikeState
  kd-recycle (st) =
    if kd-can-recycle st == False then st
    else kd-set-rest st (st.downs) (st.founds) (kd-reverse (st.waste)) [] (st.sterile + 1) (st.moves + 1)

Section: The Opponent

 There is no opponent in solitaire, so this is the player the page runs when
 you ask to watch. It is a priority order, not a search, and it is honest
 about the one judgement that separates a decent Klondike player from a bad
 one: a card sent to a foundation cannot come back cheaply, so only aces and
 twos go up unconditionally. Anything higher waits until BOTH foundations of
 the other colour have reached the rank below it, which is the standard safe
 rule and the reason this player does not bury the card it needed.

  kd-safe-to-found : KlondikeState, Integer -> Boolean
  kd-safe-to-found (st) (card) =
    let r = kd-rank card
    in if r <= 1 then True
    else if kd-red card then kd-both-at-least st 0 3 (r - 1)
    else kd-both-at-least st 1 2 (r - 1)

  kd-both-at-least : KlondikeState, Integer, Integer, Integer -> Boolean
  kd-both-at-least (st) (a) (b) (r) =
    if kd-found-at st a < r then False
    else if kd-found-at st b < r then False
    else True

 The move code packs three small numbers: `from * 10000 + start * 100 + to`.
 A start never exceeds 51 and a `to` never exceeds 10, so nothing collides.

  kd-encode : Integer, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  kd-encode (from) (start) (to) = from * 10000 + start * 100 + to

  kd-decode : Integer -> KlondikeMove
  kd-decode (code) =
    let from = code / 10000
    in let rem = rng-mod code 10000
    in let start = rem / 100
    in let to = rng-mod rem 100
    in KlondikeMove { from = from, start = start, to = to }

  kd-suggest : KlondikeState -> Integer
  kd-suggest (st) =
    let a = kd-find-foundation st 0
    in if a >= 0 then a
    else let b = kd-find-flip st 0
    in if b >= 0 then b
    else let c = kd-find-from-waste st 0
    in if c >= 0 then c
    else kd-find-foundation-any st 0

 The safe rule above holds a card back so it is still there for the tableau.
 When there is nothing else left to do at all, holding it back stops the
 game instead of protecting it, so the last tier sends anything up that will
 go. It cannot loop: this player never takes a card OFF a foundation, so
 every move this tier makes is one the game cannot undo.

  kd-find-foundation-any : KlondikeState, Integer -> Integer
  kd-find-foundation-any (st) (i) =
    if i >= 8 then (-1)
    else let from = if i == 0 then 7 else i - 1
    in let start = kd-top-index st from
    in let head = kd-move-head st from start
    in if head < 0 then kd-find-foundation-any st (i + 1)
    else let s = kd-suit head
    in if kd-can-move st from start (s + 7) then kd-encode from start (s + 7)
    else kd-find-foundation-any st (i + 1)

 Anything that can safely go up, from the waste first and then the tableau.

  kd-find-foundation : KlondikeState, Integer -> Integer
  kd-find-foundation (st) (i) =
    if i >= 8 then (-1)
    else let from = if i == 0 then 7 else i - 1
    in let start = kd-top-index st from
    in let head = kd-move-head st from start
    in if head < 0 then kd-find-foundation st (i + 1)
    else if kd-safe-to-found st head == False then kd-find-foundation st (i + 1)
    else let s = kd-suit head
    in if kd-can-move st from start (s + 7) then kd-encode from start (s + 7)
    else kd-find-foundation st (i + 1)

  kd-top-index : KlondikeState, Integer -> Integer
  kd-top-index (st) (from) =
    if from >= 7 then 0
    else list-length (kd-get-col st from) - 1

 A tableau move that turns a card over. The run must start exactly where the
 face-down cards end, or the move leaves something still covering them.

  kd-find-flip : KlondikeState, Integer -> Integer
  kd-find-flip (st) (c) =
    if c >= 7 then (-1)
    else let d = kd-down-at st c
    in if d == 0 then kd-find-flip st (c + 1)
    else let n = list-length (kd-get-col st c)
    in if n <= d then kd-find-flip st (c + 1)
    else let m = kd-find-target st c d 0
    in if m >= 0 then m
    else kd-find-flip st (c + 1)

  kd-find-target : KlondikeState, Integer, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  kd-find-target (st) (from) (start) (to) =
    if to >= 7 then (-1)
    else if kd-can-move st from start to then kd-encode from start to
    else kd-find-target st from start (to + 1)

  kd-find-from-waste : KlondikeState, Integer -> Integer
  kd-find-from-waste (st) (to) =
    if to >= 7 then (-1)
    else if kd-can-move st 7 0 to then kd-encode 7 0 to
    else kd-find-from-waste st (to + 1)

 There is deliberately no "move a king to a space" rule here beyond what the
 three above already reach. A king that sits on face-down cards is moved by
 the flip rule, and one that comes off the waste is moved by the waste rule;
 what is left is shuffling a king between two empty spaces, which changes
 nothing and is the cheapest infinite loop in this game.

 What the page's watch mode asks for: a move code, or -2 meaning turn the
 stock, -3 meaning gather the waste back up, or -1 meaning there is nothing
 left worth doing. The sterile count is what makes -1 reachable: it counts
 moves since anything was turned over or reached a foundation, and a player
 who has been round the whole pack twice without either has finished.

  kd-ai : KlondikeState -> Integer
  kd-ai (st) =
    if kd-won st then (-1)
    else if st.sterile > 120 then (-1)
    else let m = kd-suggest st
    in if m >= 0 then m
    else if kd-can-draw st then (-2)
    else if kd-can-recycle st then (-3)
    else (-1)

Section: Game Runner

  klondike-run : Integer, Integer -> KlondikeResult
  klondike-run (seed) (draw) =
    let st = klondike-new seed draw
    in kd-play-loop st 0

  kd-play-loop : KlondikeState, Integer -> KlondikeResult
  kd-play-loop (st) (steps) =
    if steps >= 600 then kd-result st
    else let m = kd-ai st
    in if m == (-1) then kd-result st
    else if m == (-2) then kd-play-loop (kd-draw st) (steps + 1)
    else if m == (-3) then kd-play-loop (kd-recycle st) (steps + 1)
    else let mv = kd-decode m
    in kd-play-loop (kd-apply-move st (mv.from) (mv.start) (mv.to)) (steps + 1)

  kd-result : KlondikeState -> KlondikeResult
  kd-result (st) =
    KlondikeResult { founded = kd-founded st 0 0, moves = st.moves, won = kd-won st }
